cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use repository-authored InclusiveShift-HAR software, cite this
  metadata and cite every third-party dataset separately under its own terms.
title: >-
  InclusiveShift-HAR: Annotation-Isolated Wearable Activity Evaluation and
  Participant-Level Reproducibility Evidence
type: software
version: 0.1.7a0
repository-code: https://github.com/abdullahuseyinli-dot/inclusive-shift-har
authors:
  - family-names: Huseyinli
    given-names: Abdulla
abstract: >-
  Research software for participant-exclusive wearable activity evaluation,
  annotation-isolated signal preprocessing and explicit inference-population
  contracts. Opened datasets retain development, stress-test, diagnostic or
  historical consumed roles. Negative model outcomes, failures and superseded
  evidence remain visible. InclusiveHAR trial boundaries are unrecoverable;
  this software does not establish clinical validity, state-of-the-art
  performance or independent confirmation of later inventions.
keywords:
  - human activity recognition
  - wearable sensing
  - inertial sensors
  - domain generalization
  - participant-exclusive evaluation
  - annotation leakage
  - reproducible research
license: Apache-2.0
notes: >-
  Apache-2.0 applies only to repository-authored material that the copyright
  holder has authority to license. Third-party datasets, legacy coursework
  artifacts, predictions, checkpoints, papers, and figures retain their original
  terms, including IMU-HAR-IL's CC BY-NC 4.0 restriction. The package version
  remains the current development version, not a new release or tag. Final
  release metadata requires owner approval and an actual immutable commit;
  no DOI, acceptance status or Zenodo publication is asserted.
